------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SCOPE OF THIS RELEASE
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This repository contains the statistical analysis code supporting the
publication "Computable longitudinal patient journeys derived from structured
and unstructured EHR data: development, validation, and clinical application in
GLP-1 receptor agonist therapy" (Nature Medicine, 2026): cohort construction,
persistence-of-therapy censoring, generalized estimating equation trajectory
models and Cox proportional hazards time-to-threshold models.

The grant in the LICENSE file covers this code only.

It does not extend to the RespondHealth extraction platform, comprising the
agentic extraction pipeline, the verification and fine-tuned extraction models,
and the knowledge graph construction code. That platform is proprietary, is not
distributed here, and is described in the paper's Code availability statement as
unavailable for commercial reasons. No part of it is required to read or reuse
the code in this repository, which consumes a prepared analytic dataset and does
not call the platform.

It does not extend to the underlying electronic health record data, which are
licensed from Harris Computer Systems and cannot be redistributed. See the paper's
Data availability statement for the terms under which de-identified
individual-level data may be requested.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
DATA INCLUDED IN THIS REPOSITORY
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

None. No patient-level data, aggregate data or intermediate analytic output is
distributed with this code. The .gitignore is written to keep it that way. The
code is published so that every analytic decision behind the reported results
can be read and checked; it cannot be executed against the data reported in the
paper.

The regression tests in tests/ run standalone and require no study data.
